  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "With a string `n` representing an integer, output *the closest integer (not including itself), which is a palindrome*. If there is a tie, output ***the smaller one***.\n\nThe closest is defined as the absolute difference minimized between two integers.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: n = \"123\"\nOutput: \"121\"\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: n = \"1\"\nOutput: \"0\"\nExplanation: 0 and 2 are the closest palindromes but we return the smallest which is 0.\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= n.length <= 18`\n* `n` is composed of only digits.\n* `n` does not have leading zeros.\n* `n` is representing an integer in the range `[1, 1018 - 1]`.",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
